{"timestamp":"2026-09-14T08:43:03.861Z","ordinal":474,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a09f05-65f8-7b43-8c85-62bb0bcdc6a6","turn_id":"01a09f10-f1d7-76f0-a811-ce00bc7a723c","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-8e53e94c-b7d9-4c5c-9174-35e2a3ee36ba","process_id":"28724","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","cat /home/chirurgie/.cache/q3-native-order-live-20260914.context-report-corrected.json"],"cwd":"file:///mnt/hdd01/Soft/GitHub/chen_q3_rh_clean","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat /home/chirurgie/.cache/q3-native-order-live-20260914.context-report-corrected.json","name":"q3-native-order-live-20260914.context-report-corrected.json","path":"/home/chirurgie/.cache/q3-native-order-live-20260914.context-report-corrected.json"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"{\"actual_behavior\":\"The cold-entry agent used a JavaScript wrapper that called tools.exec_command and emitted only r.output. The first wrapper exposed plan text but discarded inner status fields; the primary CommandExecution event later records exit_code 2 and FATAL:WRITER_LOCK_COLLISION. The retry wrapper slept 30 seconds and emitted only Script completed with empty Output; the agent then treated the missing wrapper metadata as proof that no running session or poll was required. The primary retry event later records exit_code 2 and HOLD, but that retrospective event does not make the contemporaneous inference supported.\",\"affected_operations\":[\"workflow-team-observe-native\"],\"assignment_id\":\"TEAM_NATIVE_CONTEXT_REPORT_20260914\",\"attempt_id\":\"attempt-20260914-context-01\",\"base_commit\":\"83d3cc95594e9c9847be987beb1a72ec6b0bebbd\",\"evidence\":[{\"locator\":\"docs/session_protocols/team-evidence-01d76eb6f9c90c223419b9b0f78b24afe04bc6eee16332bcdec558bdac9bc0e3.bin\",\"sha256\":\"01d76eb6f9c90c223419b9b0f78b24afe04bc6eee16332bcdec558bdac9bc0e3\"},{\"locator\":\"docs/session_protocols/team-evidence-7d73d70e31d8524b91c21030f6ee1a1fe956ab7ee863206d6b9bf9c7c8b26b9b.bin\",\"sha256\":\"7d73d70e31d8524b91c21030f6ee1a1fe956ab7ee863206d6b9bf9c7c8b26b9b\"}],\"expected_behavior\":\"Observation wrappers must retain and inspect the complete exec_command result, including output, exit_code, session_id or live-session state, and chunk metadata. An outer Script completed message or empty output alone must leave child completion and absence of a live session UNKNOWN. Native evidence must be recorded only with exact provider/readback evidence; writer-lock collision and observer-only task mismatch must remain fail-closed.\",\"expected_rule_source\":{\"locator\":\"docs/CODEX_CONTROL.md\",\"sha256\":\"9a28b04e5d898550b39014cf6d28ca510940e0dbaba26461d1313f7ab8fbae00\"},\"input_paths\":[{\"path\":\"docs/CODEX_CONTROL.md\",\"sha256\":\"9a28b04e5d898550b39014cf6d28ca510940e0dbaba26461d1313f7ab8fbae00\"},{\"path\":\"docs/Codex/TEAM_RUNTIME_REFACTOR_PLAN_2026-09-11.md\",\"sha256\":\"342746ed3fbfec1c610f4e202116928832ecb7db6b81df83e831e7d6c5deece5\"},{\"path\":\"docs/cartographer/TOOLS.yaml\",\"sha256\":\"5b328ac6f78badacb45d1468a09e92a05c5b2ef3a734003c727ba3118687f9cd\"},{\"path\":\"orchestrator/startup_runtime.py\",\"sha256\":\"cdb0cfeaaa6ba1ec1828fedf107887b31b5a2791feaffb61ddffa74f95fbfd49\"},{\"path\":\"orchestrator/team_records.py\",\"sha256\":\"209921fd0f21b0297e2bfc09453f7d85f7dc1a0aa008fd9ad3b8bc38e01d6339\"},{\"path\":\"orchestrator/tests/test_workflow_runtime.py\",\"sha256\":\"a9e5c5ac85237df61918e58b1ff0af8affb201cdb5b17030a0d7b00cad170df2\"},{\"path\":\"orchestrator/workflow_runtime.py\",\"sha256\":\"69bf0d9023fac19ee48fc9c7849083ce13a7d7c735c9cb839d86f143523a3347\"}],\"observed_at\":\"2026-09-14T10:31:22+02:00\",\"reporter_host\":\"local\",\"reporter_task\":\"/root/native_context_report\",\"reproduction\":\"Use the recorded wrappers: const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd: \\\"pwd && sed -n '1,240p' SESSION_ENTRY.md && python3 orchestrator/workflow_runtime.py plan\\\", workdir: \\\"/mnt/hdd01/Soft/GitHub/chen_q3_rh_clean\\\", yield_time_ms: 30000, max_output_tokens: 20000}); text(r.output); then const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd: \\\"sleep 30\\\\npython3 orchestrator/workflow_runtime.py plan\\\", workdir: \\\"/mnt/hdd01/Soft/GitHub/chen_q3_rh_clean\\\", yield_time_ms: 30000, max_output_tokens: 16000}); text(r.output); observe that the outer wrapper exposes only output while the complete inner result is not retained, so completion/session status cannot be inferred from the outer cell result.\",\"schema\":\"q3_issue_report.v1\",\"severity\":\"MEDIUM\",\"subject_id\":\"cold-entry-exec-wrapper-status-20260911\",\"subject_type\":\"agent-context-tool-status\",\"suspected_class\":\"AGENT_CONTEXT_ERROR\",\"uncertainty\":\"The standalone outer functions.exec return object with its discarded fields was not retained, so the historical presence or absence of a live child session at the retry inference boundary cannot be reconstructed. The later rollout item-completed event establishes that the command eventually ended with exit_code 2 and HOLD; it does not establish what metadata was available to the agent at the time of inference. Writer-lock collision and owner installation/task mismatch are independently evidenced expected guards, not a canonical code defect; no source repair or lock relaxation is supported by this report.\"}\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"{\"actual_behavior\":\"The cold-entry agent used a JavaScript wrapper that called tools.exec_command and emitted only r.output. The first wrapper exposed plan text but discarded inner status fields; the primary CommandExecution event later records exit_code 2 and FATAL:WRITER_LOCK_COLLISION. The retry wrapper slept 30 seconds and emitted only Script completed with empty Output; the agent then treated the missing wrapper metadata as proof that no running session or poll was required. The primary retry event later records exit_code 2 and HOLD, but that retrospective event does not make the contemporaneous inference